  "question_form": "state is the observed corrupted form; choose which candidate is its root",
  "decoy_rule": "on the ranked layers, the most character-similar other roots (Dice bigram coefficient), one formula across the alphabetic arms; the IME layer's candidates come from the reading index instead -- the characters sharing the reading of the errored position -- and the unrelated-form control (L4) draws a shuffled sample of the pool",
  "validity_constraint": "on the ranked layers (L2, L3del, L3) an item is kept only if the root is the closest candidate to the state under the arm's measure, so every retained item has a positive margin; the constraint does NOT apply to L1 (other attested error realisations of the same root -- not ranked, not decoys) or to L4 (a shuffled sample of the pool -- the unrelated-form control, where the root is not expected to be nearest). For the IME layer (L2c) the candidates are homophones by construction, so a similarity margin is 0 or 1 throughout and is recorded as null; that layer's difficulty is measured instead, by `group_size` (how many characters the channel offers for the reading) and `group_rank` (where in that group the root falls when the group is ordered by corpus frequency, which is the order an input method actually presents). Applying the constraint to every layer without this scoping cut rrc-zh from 12,351 items to 294.",
